1. bits of a number: $substr<165, 7, 4, fmt=08b> $substr<165, 3, 0, fmt=08b>
2. a single bit (lsb omitted): $substr<165, 0, fmt=08b>
3. hex digits: $substr<48879, 3, 2, fmt=x>
4. text, from the right: $substr<Hello world, 4, 0>
5. characters, not bytes: $substr<héllo, 3, 1>
6. a real number: $substr<3.14159, 3, 0, fmt=.2f>
7. padded text (escaped >): [$substr<abc, 4, 0, fmt=\>5>]
8. str is expanded first: $substr<$repeat(text=ab, count=3), 4, 2>
9. escaped commas: $substr<a\, b\, c, 5, 3>
